[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Orthodox Defense, Main Line"]
[ECO "D63"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "pin-on-f6,c-file-pressure"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2...e6"]
[Start "orthodox 3.Nc3"]

3... Nf6 ( 3... Be7 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Bg5 ) 4. Bg5 { Pins the knight on f6 to the queen. If it moves, White takes on d5 with more force. [%cal Gg5f6] } 4... Be7 ( 4... Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. Nf3 Qa5 7. Nd2 { The Cambridge Springs pin on c3 needs an answer. The knight on d2 unpins the bishop's line and guards the knight on c3. } 7... Bb4 8. Qc2 { Guards the knight on c3 again and keeps Black from winning it. } ) 5. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1 and backs up d4, so the centre is solid before the pieces come out. } 5... O-O ( 5... h6 6. Bh4 O-O 7. Nf3 ) 6. Nf3 { Develops and guards d4 and e5, so Black has no easy way to break the centre. } 6... Nbd7 ( 6... h6 7. Bh4 ) 7. Rc1 { Puts the rook on the c-file ahead of time. When the c-pawns trade, the rook is already there. } 7... c6 ( 7... dxc4 8. Bxc4 c5 9. O-O ) 8. Bd3 { Aims at h7 and waits: if Black takes on c4, the bishop recaptures with a gain of time. } 8... dxc4 9. Bxc4 { Retakes the pawn and puts the bishop back on a good diagonal. } 9... Nd5 10. Bxe7 { Trades off the bishop that was pinning, so White has fewer problems with Black's extra space. } 10... Qxe7 11. O-O { Castles. The king is safe and the rook on f1 can support e4 later. } 11... Nxc3 12. Rxc3 { Recaptures with the rook, which stays on the open c-file where it presses on c6 and c7. } 12... e5 13. Qc2 { Plan: pile up on the c-file and keep the pieces coordinated. If Black pushes e5, take it and aim at the weak pawn on c6. } *
